# .env.example — secret NAMES only. Never put a value in this file; it is committed.
#
# One `NAME=` line per secret the project needs (empty right-hand side), e.g. `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=`.
# `orche secret run -- <cmd>` reads the names listed here, fetches each value from the project's
# backend (GCP Secret Manager / Vercel / keychain cache) and injects it into <cmd>'s
# environment only. Missing ones: `orche secret missing dev`, then
# `orche secret request NAME --env dev,prod --why "<purpose>" --how <issuer URL>`.
